@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the durable proveo home — what it holds, who writes it, and what is never mounted
' covers: internal/proveohome/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: internal/run/run.go (homeLine)
' covers: internal/run/home_line_test.go
'
' WHAT THE RUN SAYS ABOUT THE HOME (F15, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17; the user: "Print
' what sbx sees (Recommended)"). The old line, "proveo home: <root> (mounted at
' /proveo-home)", described the deleted docker backend. MEASURED:
' internal/run/run.go homeLine(root, man.Home) (:432-446) prints "proveo home:
' <root> (the sandbox sees <rel>, <rel>, …, toolchains at their host paths)" —
' each declared home.mounts[].host relative dir, then "toolchains" ("at its
' host path" when it is the only one). It does NOT list linkedDirs, which are
' computed later in the run. Pinned by TestTheHomeLineNamesWhatTheSandboxSees
' (internal/run/home_line_test.go). The container-side diagram below (HOME=
' /proveo-home, `-v $PROVEO_HOME:/proveo-home`) is the docker backend's, kept as
' HISTORY; on sbx each declared dir is bound at its own host path. OpenCode's
' share is no longer mounted (D2, _spec/defs/opencode/engine-local-history.puml).
title Proveo home — durable session state without binding host IDE homes

actor "Developer" as DEV

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  folder "PROVEO_HOME\n~/.proveo (0700)" as ROOT <<host>>
  database "cursor/.cursor\nclaudecode/.claude\nopencode/{config,share}" as STATE <<db>>
  component "internal/proveohome\nRoot · Prepare · ResumeArgs" as PH <<app>>
  component "internal/runner\ndocker argv" as RUN <<app>>
  folder "Host IDE homes\n~/.cursor · ~/.claude" as IDE <<error>>
}

node "Agent container (--rm)" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "HOME=/proveo-home" as CHOME <<app>>
  component "agent CLI\nwrites session transcripts" as AGENT <<app>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN PH : " ""proveo run <target>"" "
PH ARROW_MAIN ROOT : mkdir 0700 per\n""home.mounts[].host""
PH ARROW_ERROR STATE : scrub ""home.mounts[].deny""\nbefore every run
ROOT ARROW_MAIN STATE
PH ARROW_MAIN RUN : Plan{Mounts, Env}
RUN ARROW_MAIN CHOME : " ""-v $PROVEO_HOME:/proveo-home"" \n ""-e HOME=/proveo-home"" "
CHOME ARROW_MAIN AGENT
AGENT ARROW_MAIN STATE : sessions persist\npast container exit
PH ARROW_ERROR IDE : never mounted

note right of PH
  **Why a proveo-owned home**
  Container is ""--rm"": without a durable mount every
  session, auth cache and seeded config dies with it.
  Binding the host IDE home instead would expose the
  developer's real credentials to an autonomous agent.

  **The scrub is a security control**
  ""home.mounts[].deny"" lists auth basenames (e.g.
  ""auth.json"") removed from the host dir *before* the
  bind. A login token minted inside one sandbox cannot
  accumulate in the durable cache and be reused by the
  next run. Basenames only — path separators and
  ""."" / "".."" are ignored, so a manifest cannot escape
  its own subdir.

  **Fixed container path — DOCKER ONLY**
  ""ContainerHome = /proveo-home"" — that backend runs the
  agent as an arbitrary HOST uid (""--user 501:20""), so HOME
  must not depend on the image's baked passwd entry.

  **sbx sets no HOME.** It runs its own agent user
  (uid 1000), mounts the session volumes under that user's
  home and has its credential proxy write ""\.credentials\.json""
  there. Redirecting HOME orphaned all three: the agent read
  the stale MOUNTED credential instead of the live
  proxy-managed one and reported "Not logged in". The proveo
  home is still MOUNTED on that backend — only the env
  redirect is gone. See sbxHome and ladder_test.go rung 3.
end note

note bottom of STATE
  Reclaimed only by ""proveo clean --homes"".
  Routine ""proveo clean"" leaves this tree alone —
  see _spec/internal/clean/clean-lifecycle.puml
end note

' --- IGNORE: layout hints (do not edit) ---
HOST -down[hidden]- CTR
' --- END IGNORE ---
@enduml
